        "point": "Dismantling the '5 Similar / 5 Contrary' construct",
        "detail": "Explain that the supposed 10 transitions include unequal hierarchical weights. In Measure 1, beat 5 is a surface passing tone (diminution) leading into the downbeat harmonic arrival of Measure 2. In tonal and theatrical counterpoint, passing tones prolong the underlying harmony and do not instantiate independent contrapuntal motions. Counting beat 4->5 and 5->0 as two separate occurrences is akin to counting an accented passing tone as two separate harmonies."
      },
